#: src/quick-start/installation.md:128
msgid ""
"For temporary runs the repo builds a standalone binary. Clone and build it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:137
msgid ""
"This produces the `rut` binary at `target/release/rut`. Put it on your "
"`PATH` (or call it by path — the pages here use the bare name):"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:142
msgid "\"$PWD/target/release:$PATH\""
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:143
msgid ""
"# usage: rut — run <dir | mod.rutbundle> [--fuel N] [--symbols "
"<file.rutsym>] | fmt <file.rut | dir> [--check] | pack <dir> [-o "
"out.rutbundle] [--strip] | fetch <dir> | dump <file.rut>\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:147
msgid ""
"The binary embeds the whole engine: lexer, parser, compiler, typed bytecode, "
"and the VM. The toolchain's standard packages (`core`, `pouch`, `ink`, "
"`json`, …) ship as compiled `.rutbundle`s on jsDelivr — a program says `use "
"ink::{ Logger };` and its manifest's `deps` row mounts the package from the "
"CDN, pinned by sha256 ([dependency "
"kinds](../reference/dependency-kinds.md)), since every rut program is a "
"module directory ([your first rut program](first-program.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:156
msgid "Try it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:160
msgid ""
"<<'EOF'\n"
"// hello/rut.jsonc — the manifest IS the program's door\n"
"{\n"
"  \"name\": \"hello\",\n"
"  \"entry\": { \"lib\": \"./main.rut\" },\n"
"  \"deps\": {\n"
"    // ink — the toolchain's logger package, served by jsDelivr at the\n"
"    // std-v5 tag, pinned by sha256\n"
"    \"ink\": { \"url\": "
"\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/hpp2334/rut@std-v5/dist/std/ink.rutbundle\", "
"\"sha256\": "
"\"200ab1ea41bee7145d20c0665f799302436dcbe82bdab8858c7c74708d1b306a\" }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"EOF\n"
"cat > hello/main.rut <<'EOF'\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"hello\");\n"
"    log.info(f\"hello, rut!\");\n"
"}\n"
"EOF\n"
"rut run hello\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:187
msgid ""
"The first run fetched `ink` from jsDelivr into `hello/.rut/cache`; `rut "
"fetch hello` pre-warms that cache without running anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/installation.md:190
msgid ""
"If that printed, the CLI is ready. Continue to [your first rut "
"program](first-program.md) — and keep the lane's role in mind: the CLI is "
"for **temporary runs** (`run`, `fmt`, `dump`, `pack`), not a shipping path. "
"Real projects depend on the crates and embed the engine; [the rut "
"CLI](../reference/cli.md) is the binary's reference."
msgstr ""

