#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:3
msgid ""
"rut feels like TypeScript on the surface and Rust underneath the hood. This "
"page walks one program through the whole toolchain — running, formatting, "
"inspecting, and budgeting — so every later page can assume the workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:8
msgid "Write and run"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:10
msgid ""
"This chapter drives everything through the temporary-run `rut` CLI — the "
"fastest lane for learning the language ([installation](installation.md)). A "
"real project embeds the engine instead and calls it from Rust ([embedding "
"and native modules](../reference/embedding.md)); the language, the types, "
"and the workflow below are the same either way."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:16
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"hello\");\n"
"    let name = \"rut\";\n"
"    log.info(f\"hello, {name}!\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:26
msgid ""
"Every rut program is a **module directory**: a `rut.jsonc` naming the "
"package and its dependencies, plus the source file the manifest points at. "
"Create it and run the directory:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:32
msgid ""
"<<'EOF'\n"
"// hello/rut.jsonc — the manifest IS the program's door\n"
"{\n"
"  \"name\": \"hello\",\n"
"  \"entry\": { \"lib\": \"./main.rut\" },\n"
"  \"deps\": {\n"
"    // ink — the toolchain's logger package, served by jsDelivr at the\n"
"    // std-v5 tag, pinned by sha256\n"
"    \"ink\": { \"url\": "
"\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/hpp2334/rut@std-v5/dist/std/ink.rutbundle\", "
"\"sha256\": "
"\"200ab1ea41bee7145d20c0665f799302436dcbe82bdab8858c7c74708d1b306a\" }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"EOF\n"
"# save the program above as hello/main.rut, then:\n"
"rut run hello\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:52
msgid ""
"The run works from ANY directory — nothing about it assumes a clone of the "
"toolchain's repo. The url row names the package on jsDelivr; the CLI fetches "
"it once into the project's cache (`.rut/cache`), every later run is a pure "
"cache hit, and `rut fetch hello` pre-warms the cache without running "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:58
msgid "Three things to notice:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:60
msgid ""
"**One directory with a `rut.jsonc` is one program.** The manifest is the "
"runnable unit — `rut run <dir>` (or a packed `.rutbundle`) is the only run "
"lane. Inside the package, one file is one module; cross-module code is "
"reached through `use` paths (see the [modules "
"tutorial](../tutorial/modules.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:65
msgid ""
"**`use ink::{ Logger };`** pulls `Logger` out of the `ink` package — and the "
"manifest's `deps` row is what mounts it: a `use` line says _which_ names the "
"program wants, the manifest says _where_ the package lives ([project "
"structure](../reference/project-structure.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:69
msgid ""
"**`f\"hello, {name}!\"`** is a format literal: `{expr}` interpolates any "
"expression, rendered through the value's display contract."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:72
msgid "`entry fn main()` is the entry the CLI calls."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:74
msgid "Values, briefly"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:76
msgid "Extend the file — rut infers, and every type is known at compile time:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:78
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"hello\");\n"
"    let n = 10;            // i32 — the integer default\n"
"    let scale = 1.5;       // f32 — the float default\n"
"    let big: u64 = 10;     // u64 via annotation — fits the default\n"
"    let flags = [1, 2, 3]; // [i32] — a fixed heap cell\n"
"    let mut sum = 0;       // `mut` — this one is written to\n"
"    for (let x of flags) {\n"
"        sum += x * n;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"sum={sum} scale={scale}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start/first-program.md:99
msgid ""
"The full tour — suffixes, casts, strings, `bytes`, structs — is the [values "
"and variables](../tutorial/values-and-variables.md) tutorial, and the exact "
"rules live in [literals and "
"inference](../reference/literals-and-inference.md)."
msgstr ""

