#: src/reference/host-fns.md:51
msgid "The surface grammar"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:53
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"host fn name(params) -> T;            // concrete signature; generics are a\n"
"                                      // compile error — a generic "
"parameter\n"
"                                      // has no shape the boundary checks\n"
"host struct Name { fields }           // flat record; every field a "
"crossing\n"
"                                      // type; no methods, no field\n"
"                                      // initializers — the shape IS the\n"
"                                      // whole surface\n"
"prelude builtin fn name<T>(params) -> T;   // engine fn, compiler-lowered\n"
"prelude builtin class Name<T> { .. }       // engine type member contract\n"
"                                           // (the closed async pair among\n"
"                                           // them — `Future<T>`, "
"`RunContext`)\n"
"prelude builtin impl i32 { .. }            // engine methods on a primitive\n"
"pub builtin class Name<T> { .. }           // the import-gated twin (below)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:71
msgid ""
"**The crossing set** — `host fn` signatures are concrete over: nil, the "
"primitives, `str`, `bytes`, and `opaque`. Returns may additionally use the "
"answer optionals `?str` / `?bytes` / `?opaque`. Named records never cross — "
"a `host struct` decl is surface, not a signature type — and the "
"anonymous-tuple lane belongs to the `entry fn` surface ([value "
"boundary](value-boundary.md)). Everything else (user classes, `Vec<T>`, "
"`[T]`, interface-typed values, closures) is a compile error on the "
"declaration."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:79
msgid ""
"**`any` is not in the language.** An `any` spelling fails at resolution as "
"an unknown type — there is no `any` type to write. Seal polymorphic values "
"with `opaque(v)` / `opaque.downcast<T>(v)` ([opaque](opaque.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:83
msgid ""
"**`builtin` is the engine's reservation** — spelled only in the toolchain's "
"own decl files (`core`, `calc`). A `builtin` in an embedder decl is a "
"compile error. The engine's contracts are spellings on types: the bracket "
"markers on inherent impl members and the closed `builtin class` pair; "
"library polymorphism stays plain `interface` ([interfaces](interfaces.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:89
msgid ""
"**`builtin` is a contextual keyword**: `.d.rut`\\-only; elsewhere it is a "
"legal identifier."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:92
msgid "The two builtin spellings"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:94
msgid ""
"A `builtin` decl spells one of two strict forms — a bare `builtin` diagnoses "
"_\"`builtin` must be spelled `prelude builtin` (ambient) or `pub builtin` "
"(import-gated)\"_:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:98
msgid ""
"**`prelude builtin`** — the **ambient** engine surface: the name binds in "
"every compilation unit, no `use` needed. The primitives and their `builtin "
"impl` methods, `opaque`, `StackTrace`, and "
"`panic`/`string_join`/`capture_stacktrace` are all ambient."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:102
msgid ""
"**`pub builtin`** — the **import-gated** engine surface: the name resolves "
"only through `use core::{ .. }`, the way a package's names do. Today's rows "
"are the closed async pair — `Future<T>`, `RunContext` — the disposal "
"context, `DisposalContext`, and the weak reference, `Weak<T>` "
"([interfaces](interfaces.md), [async and await](async.md), [the Rc "
"heap](rc-heap.md), [weak references](weak-refs.md)). The engine's weave "
"never consults the gate — it keys on the engine symbols — so a module with "
"no imports still iterates, awaits, and launches; only spelling a name in "
"source gates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:113
msgid ""
"Using a `pub builtin` name without the use line is a resolution miss that "
"names the fix, never a bare \"unknown name\":"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:120
msgid ""
"The split is per name: a unit that imports one gated name still sees every "
"ambient name for free, and an unused name in a `use core` line stays a lint, "
"not an error."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/host-fns.md:124
msgid ""
"**`opaque` wraps native state; there is no host class.** rut wraps the "
"handle in a class of its own — the wrapper-class pattern ([native containers "
"API surface](native-containers.md)). Destructors still run "
"deterministically: when a box's rc hits 0, the payload's finalize hook runs, "
"then Rust `Drop` ([the Rc heap](rc-heap.md))."
msgstr ""

