#: src/reference/stdlib.md:401
msgid ""
"`async_host` declares the engine rows (`__launch`, `__abort`, `__sleep`, "
"`__sleep_yield`); `futures` restores the typed surface: `launch_future(f: "
"Future<T>) -> LaunchedFutureHandle<T>`, `LaunchedFutureHandle.abort() -> "
"bool`, `sleep(ms: u32) -> Future<nil>`. Each embedder offers `rut/futures` "
"(a `rut_native::tree_pkg` walk) and installs `rut_std::async_host::pkg()` on "
"the chain; a world that offers neither has no launcher ([launched "
"futures](launched-futures.md), [host futures](host-futures.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:409
msgid ""
"`http_host` declares the transport rows (three async, five sync readbacks); "
"`http` wraps them in `HttpClient` / `RequestBuilder` / `Request` / "
"`Response` / `ByteStream` — async only at the points that really wait:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:414
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use http::{ HttpClient, ClientQueryMethod };\n"
"\n"
"let resp = await HttpClient.new().request()\n"
"    .method(ClientQueryMethod.Post)\n"
"    .url(\"https://example.com/api\")\n"
"    .header(\"Accept\", \"application/json\")\n"
"    .body(payload)\n"
"    .build()\n"
"    .send(cx);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:426
msgid ""
"`send` resolves at headers; `body(cx)` drains the wire; "
"`byte_stream()`/`next(cx)` walk it in chunks. Status `0` is reserved for "
"transport failure. The reqwest lane is native-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:430
msgid "Offering"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:432
msgid ""
"`core` auto-rides — every run's `.compile()` offers the core prelude unless "
"a pkg named `core` was offered. `calc` and the async pair are ordinary tree "
"packages: the host offers them (`rut_native::tree_pkg(..)`) when the "
"program's surface names them, and binds the bodies (`rut_std::math::pkg()`, "
"`rut_std::async_host::pkg()`) on the chain ([embedding](embedding.md)). The "
"`rut` CLI offers the tree packages a loose file names by `use` ([the rut "
"CLI](cli.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:440
msgid ""
"`inline = true` packages (ink, pouch, nmapset, json, strbuild, futures) are "
"source-inlined into each consumer — required for class-method surfaces, "
"whose inherent impls cross no module link boundary yet ([the "
"frontend](frontend.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:444
msgid ""
"Generic exports link on their own: instantiation happens where the body "
"lives, consumers request it, and `Vec<i64>` is one type program-wide ([the "
"compiler pipeline](compiler.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:3
msgid ""
"The frontend turns source text into a checked-syntax tree: source (UTF-8) → "
"[lexer](#the-lexer) → tokens → [parser](#the-parser) → AST, with one "
"diagnostics model flowing out of every stage. It has no type knowledge — "
"resolution and checking begin in [the compiler pipeline](compiler.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:8
msgid ""
"The implementation is three crates: `rut-lexer` (`span`, `token`, `lexer`, "
"`diag`), `rut-ast` (the arena tree and its dumper), and `rut-parser` (the "
"frame machine and its expression engine). Everything is `no_std`\\-clean and "
"wasm-compatible, so the same code runs in the CLI, the LSP, the formatter, "
"and the browser playground."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:14
msgid "The contract"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:16
msgid "Four invariants hold for any input, hostile included:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:18
msgid "invariant"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:18 src/reference/frontend.md:122
msgid "mechanism"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:20
msgid "C1"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:20
msgid ""
"**Flat AST** — nodes are records in one arena; children are `NodeId`s, never "
"boxed pointers, built bottom-up. Drop/clone are flat `Vec` ops."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:20
msgid "[AST](#the-ast)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:21
msgid "C2"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:21
msgid ""
"**No native recursion** — an explicit frame stack handles structure; "
"expressions use an iterative operator/operand engine. Host stack use is "
"constant regardless of input."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:21
msgid "[parser](#the-parser)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:22
msgid "C3"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:22
msgid ""
"**Depth budget, not stack exhaustion** — nesting over the budget is a normal "
"diagnostic, never a host crash."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:22
msgid "[budgets](#nesting-budgets)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:23
msgid "C4"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:23
msgid ""
"**Lookahead discipline** — local decisions peek at most 4 tokens; the two "
"decisions that need more use read-only balancing scans. The cursor is "
"monotone non-decreasing for the whole parse, recovery included — there is no "
"checkpoint/rollback."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:23
msgid "[lookahead](#lookahead)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:25
msgid ""
"The lexer and parser are pure functions — `lex(src) -> (Vec<Token>, "
"Vec<Diag>)` and `parse(src, mode) -> (Ast, Vec<Diag>)` — so they are "
"fuzzable and reusable in an LSP or formatter with no VM present."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:29
msgid "The lexer"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:31
msgid ""
"One flat `Tok` enum for literals, punctuation, and operators. Keywords are "
"ordinary `Ident`s; the parser matches them by interner name. **Reserved "
"words are rejected by the lexer** with a message naming the rut replacement "
"(`interface`, `private`, `void`, `in`); `?.` and `??` are punctuation-level "
"rejections, a separate mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:36
msgid ""
"Maximal munch with an explicit longest-match table; `/` vs `//` vs `/*` "
"resolves with one lookahead. Compound assignment operators are one token "
"each (`+=`, `<<=`, `&&=`, …), so there is no munch ambiguity."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:39
msgid ""
"Numeric literals: `0x`/`0b`/`0o`, `_` separators, and per-width suffixes "
"(`u8..u64`, `i8..i64`, `f32`/`f64`). Unsuffixed integers default to `i32`, "
"unsuffixed floats to `f32`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:42
msgid ""
"Comments are dropped (doc comments are re-attached by the formatter's "
"gap-scan, below)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:45
msgid "Format strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:47
msgid ""
"`f\"...\"` is the one construct the lexer must understand structurally, "
"because placeholders hold expressions, not strings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:53
msgid "// decoded like a plain string; {{ }} -> { }\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:54
msgid "// a FULLY LEXED token stream, `}`-terminated\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:58
msgid ""
"The lexer enters hole mode after `{` (not `{{`), balances braces, and lexes "
"normally until depth 0. Holes are re-lexed, not stored as text, so "
"placeholder expressions carry real spans inside the literal's span. A hole "
"may contain any expression except a string literal — a quote inside a hole "
"is a lex error with a _bind it to a name first_ note. See "
"[Templates](templates.md) for the surface semantics."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:65
msgid ""
"Raw strings `r\"...\"` carry everything up to the closing `\"` literally; "
"`\\\"` inside a raw string does not close it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:68
msgid "Nesting budgets"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:70
msgid "Two budgets make C3 a law:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:72
msgid ""
"`NEST_MAX = 1024` — the lexer's bracket depth budget (`rut-lexer/span.rs`). "
"Exceeding it is one clean diagnostic at the offending opener."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:74
msgid ""
"`EXPR_MAX = 64` — the parser's expression-nesting budget. The frame machine "
"itself has no host-stack cost, but downstream recursive walks (AST dump, "
"typecheck) do; the cap keeps the trees they visit shallow."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:78
msgid ""
"Both produce the same diagnostic — _nesting too deep_ — and neither can "
"overflow the host stack."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:81
msgid "The parser"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:83
msgid "One loop over the token slice drives two mechanisms:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:85
msgid ""
"A **frame stack** handles structure — one frame kind per grammar rule "
"(`Module`, `Item`, `Block`, `TypeArgList`, `Pattern`, `Arm`, `Impl`, …). A "
"rule that needs a child pushes a frame; a completed frame pops and hands its "
"`NodeId` to the parent."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:89
msgid ""
"An embedded **Pratt engine** handles expressions — an operator stack plus an "
"operand stack of `NodeId`s. Binary and assignment steps push an operator; "
"reductions pop operands and push one node, bottom-up."
msgstr ""

