#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:164
msgid "The mount law — four passes, one gate"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:166
msgid ""
"All loader-owned; the session stays I/O-free and the compile graph never "
"learns what a peer is."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:169
msgid ""
"**The `deps` walk — unchanged.** Recursive, name order, first-mount-wins, "
"cycle guard, name-mismatch error. While walking, the loader records each "
"mounted package's `peer-deps` into the session's peer registry (it reads "
"every dep's manifest anyway)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:173
msgid ""
"**The dev pass — root only.** The program root's `dev-deps` mount exactly "
"like `deps`. A dep's dev table is **never** walked — a consumer's world "
"never contains another package's dev table. Offering a package to someone "
"else's program (`rut_native::dir_pkgs`, or `.pkg(..)` by hand) is the same "
"law: it walks no dev-deps and runs no gate (its peer declarations are still "
"recorded)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:180
msgid ""
"**The peer gate — one post-closure pass.** After the full closure exists, "
"for every mounted package and every `peer-deps` entry:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:182
msgid ""
"**required**: the peer must resolve in the session, else the D1 error. Never "
"auto-pulled."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:184
msgid ""
"**optional, present** (any reason): the declarer's group file (the "
"descriptor's `lib`, an impl-only `.rut`) is appended to its `Module.source` "
"— groups in peer-name order after the base. The combined text stays one "
"source string, so every consumer of module sources (the splice, bundles, "
"wasm mounts) is untouched."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:189
msgid "**optional, absent**: inert — the group simply never mounts."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:190
msgid ""
"**paths**: the program root's own peer paths are read and name-checked even "
"when dev-deps already supplied presence — a broken path is the loud D3 "
"packaging-bug error at the package's own build. A dep's peer paths are never "
"read: presence is by name, so a broken peer path is inert for an optional "
"peer and unreachable for a required one. The gate is post-closure because a "
"peer may mount after its declarer alphabetically; groups add no package "
"names, so one pass is a fixpoint."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:199
msgid ""
"**Compile — unchanged.** The graph splices each compilation unit from its "
"origin-deduplicated leaf list (first position wins, topological order "
"preserved); in the no-collision case the composed text is byte-identical to "
"the pre-peer law."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:204
msgid ""
"**Groups are satisfaction-only.** A group file contains the peer "
"integration's wrapper families — newtype class decls and their inherent "
"impls (and private helpers); it declares no host fns and no manifest rows — "
"the base owns the interfaces and every other public name, and the wrappers "
"are the group's whole addition. This is what keeps the diagnostic matrix "
"total: the only ways to reach the integration are through the wrapper names "
"(which `use` paths route into the declaring package) or the base package's "
"interfaces, and both have dedicated peer-aware diagnostics. A group appended "
"to a module with no rut body (a `.d.rut` surface) is a load error — "
"declaration surfaces do not gate."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:216
msgid "The missing-peer matrix"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:218
msgid "case"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:220
msgid "required peer absent from the consumer's closure"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:220
msgid ""
"**D1** — loud at mount: names the package, the peer, and the fix. Not "
"silent, not auto-pulled."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:221
msgid "optional peer absent, integration never touched"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:221
msgid "nothing — silent success; that _is_ the feature"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:222
msgid "optional peer absent, integration referenced"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:222
msgid ""
"**D2** — the dedicated missing-peer diagnostic; never a bare unresolved name"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:223
msgid "peer present (any reason)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:223
msgid "the integration mounts automatically — presence-based resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:224
msgid "self-build / dev mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:224
msgid "dev-deps guarantee presence; no missing case exists"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:225
msgid "a `peer-deps` path that does not resolve"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:225
msgid ""
"**D3** — loud manifest error at the pkg's own build; for consumers, required "
"⇒ D1, optional ⇒ inert"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:227
msgid ""
"The four diagnostics, verbatim shapes (all load/resolution-time errors, "
"never runtime traps):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:230
msgid ""
"**D1** — `pkg \\`json\\` requires the peer \\`nmapset\\`, and \\`nmapset\\` "
"is not in this program's closure — peers are not pulled transitively: add "
"\"nmapset\": { \"path\": \"..\" } to your \\`rut.jsonc\\` \\`deps\\``"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:233
msgid ""
"**D2** — `cannot resolve \\`pouch\\` — \\`json\\`'s pouch integration is not "
"mounted because the optional peer \\`pouch\\` is absent from this program's "
"closure; add \"pouch\": { \"path\": \"..\" } to your \\`rut.jsonc\\` "
"\\`deps\\``. Declaring packages scan in mount order, so the diagnostic is "
"deterministic when several packages declare the same peer. Required peers "
"never reach this path — D1 fires at mount."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:239
msgid ""
"**D3** — three shapes, all _a packaging bug in json_: cannot read a manifest "
"at the peer path; the manifest there names it `other`; cannot read the group "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:242
msgid "**D4** — the cross-table collision (both texts quoted above)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:244
msgid "Interplay"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:246
msgid ""
"**Placement and the gate — the gate precedes the compile.** The peer gate "
"runs at load; the group compiles inside the declaring package's unit. Peer "
"absent ⇒ the group text was never assembled ⇒ the wrapper families are "
"nowhere in the program. Peer present ⇒ the group's wrapper classes and their "
"inherent impls compile in the declaring package — the inherent impl's one "
"home ([Interfaces and dispatch](interfaces.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:253
msgid ""
"**Structural satisfaction is the consumer-side story**: a consumer's own "
"types satisfy json's interfaces by having the members, whether or not any "
"peer mounted; what the peer gate controls is the wrapper families only — a "
"`JsonVec` spelling with `pouch` absent produces D2, never a mystery."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:258
msgid ""
"**Binary format untouched.** Group files declare no host fns (no binding "
"obligations appear or vanish), add no binary sections, and touch nothing the "
"verifier reads — the wrapper classes are ordinary program content. A "
"consumer's binary differs only by which wrappers mounted."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:263
msgid ""
"**Dev-deps are invisible to bundles-as-consumers.** A packed package carries "
"its peer groups; a consumer packing _their_ app never pulls the package's "
"dev table (pass 2 is root-only), so dev-only convenience packages cannot "
"leak into consumer worlds ([Module bundles](bundles.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:268
msgid ""
"**The LSP completes group impls unconditionally.** Peer gating is a "
"resolution-time concept the language server does not model; it embeds the "
"toolchain packages' sources and never parses manifests. Recorded as "
"accepted: the LSP is advisory; the compiler is the law."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:273
msgid "Consuming a peer-gated package"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:275
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"// an app that wants json's pouch integration\n"
"{\n"
"  \"deps\": {\n"
"    \"json\":  { \"path\": \"vendor/json\" },\n"
"    // presence is the only requirement\n"
"    \"pouch\": { \"path\": \"vendor/pouch\" }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:286
msgid ""
"The group mounts because `pouch` is anywhere in the closure — no extra "
"declaration beyond having the package. Drop the `pouch` row and `json` "
"mounts light; the first `use` naming a `JsonVec`\\-family wrapper produces "
"D2 instead of a mystery."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli.md:3
